    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10b-2020-p1.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Subtracting a negative is the same as adding the corresponding positive number, so \\[ \\begin{aligned} &1-(-2)-3-(-4) \\\\ &\\quad {}-5-(-6) \\\\ &\\quad = 1+2-3+4-5+6. \\end{aligned} \\] Now combine the terms: \\[ \\begin{aligned} &(1+2+4+6)-(3+5) \\\\ &\\quad = 13-8=5. \\end{aligned} \\]\n\nThus, D is the correct answer.",
      "hints": [
        "Turn subtraction of a negative into addition before combining terms",
        "Pair the positive and negative terms so the arithmetic stays small"
      ],
